From e3496fb5df378d3e7c077c5c29e53c73845b1308 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mystic Builder Dev <dev@mysticbuilder.local>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:51:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Game shell UI: main menu, /builder + /database routes, zero
 page scroll

The site behaved like a document: a sticky header, a footer and page
level scrollbars on every screen. Now it is an application shell - no
screen scrolls the page itself, only internal regions scroll, and the
chrome that used to live in the header/footer moved into the screens.

- New shell UI kit (src/components/menu-ui + src/lib/menu-assets.ts):
  a single asset registry where real art can be dropped in later
  (background art, nine-sliced button textures per state, panel
  texture, menu sounds) with everything defaulting to null so the
  built-in CSS look renders until then. NineSlice renders CSS
  border-image nine-patches; MenuButton swaps textures per
  interaction state via CSS variables and plays hover/click sounds
  (Awakening UI wavs shipped in public/assets) through useMenuSound
- '/' is now the game-style main menu boot screen: brand block with
  the version banner, menu column (LOADOUT [B], ITEM DATABASE [D],
  SOURCE CODE, SOURCE DATA), decorative emblem stage on the right
  (art slot) and the legal/credit block along the bottom; keyboard
  shortcuts B/D navigate
- Builder moved to /builder, item database to /database; old
  /?tab=database and /?b= links are gone (localEditPath now emits
  /builder?b=... and the loadout URL sync keeps the editor URL on
  /builder instead of rewriting it to /)
- Layout: header, footer and site-nav-links removed; html/body locked
  to h-dvh with overflow hidden so nothing can scroll the page
- Loadout stage now fills 100dvh (was calc(100vh - 102px) for the
  removed chrome) and its bottom bar folds in the version banner,
  DATABASE/MENU shortcuts and the compact legal line
- Database page owns one internal scroll region (the grid's own
  max-h/overflow was removed to avoid nested scrollbars); shared
  /b/[buildId] pages are viewport locked with an internal scroller
  and link back to /builder

Verified in the browser at 1920x1080/1280x800/1024x700: menu, builder
(with a v8 build loaded via query param), database and /b/ page all
render with document scrollHeight == clientHeight; import overlay,
menu navigation and shortcuts work; production build passes.
